[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3870755369","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116042#issuecomment-3870755369","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116042","id":3870755369,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7mtwop","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-09T10:14:29Z","updated_at":"2026-02-09T10:15:05Z","body":"When limiatations are applied, reaching the end point is not guaranteed. How close it gets depends on the algorithm. When using limiatations , CCDIK is documented as the most suitable method because it recursively applies the effects of child constraints to the parent. However, whether it reaches the end point still depends on the situation.\n\nFor cases with attached MRP, I think it's effective to first use LookAt/AimModifier to determine the forward axis, then use ChainIK from the next bone.\n\n<img width=\"1262\" height=\"723\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/13dd419f-0d01-4c46-8bc5-fdf987decf20\" />\n\n[ik-joint-offset-modified.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25180265/ik-joint-offset-modified.zip)\n\nWell, I agree that the reachability and setup for these aspects should be covered in more detail in the documentation and tutorials.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3870755369/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4349202258","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116042#issuecomment-4349202258","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116042","id":4349202258,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAzuPUg","user":{"login":"luzader","id":617962,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxNzk2Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/617962?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luzader","html_url":"https://github.com/luzader","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luzader/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luzader/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luzader/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luzader/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luzader/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luzader/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luzader/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luzader/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luzader/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-30T02:07:53Z","updated_at":"2026-04-30T02:07:53Z","body":"I've created a simpler MRP which shows that this can be caused by gaps in the bone chain. The original MRP has a very disjointed skeleton, but there are too many gaps in too many axes to see what is going on.\n\n[ik-joint-offset-bug116402-mrp2.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27227275/ik-joint-offset-bug116402-mrp2.zip)\n\n The red arm has a gap in the bone chain at the second joint, while the blue arm is fully connected. They are otherwise identical.\n\n<img width=\"1288\" height=\"626\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8795185c-35c7-4cac-b5d9-537c67822c48\" />\n\n<img width=\"1306\" height=\"634\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a2f74b75-dd39-4163-9da8-34ca6ba6cfea\" />\n\nIn godot both arms have CCKID solvers with the same configuration and the same target, the green sphere. The joints are constrained to rotation in Z, Z and X respectively.  The blue arm has reached the target correctly, while the red arm has reached a position above the target which appears to be the same displacement as the gap between the bones.\n\n<img width=\"1408\" height=\"858\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/881c97ca-0135-49bb-a392-cfc8669b37df\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4349202258/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4351266882","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116042#issuecomment-4351266882","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116042","id":4351266882,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABA1sQQg","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-30T09:26:02Z","updated_at":"2026-04-30T12:59:41Z","body":"As long as the same restrictions apply, Blender should behave the similar result (don't reach the goal), although there are differences in the interpretation of bone rest regarding unconnected bones.\n\n<img width=\"1145\" height=\"1074\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5c52feeb-a388-4568-8697-04aa699867cd\" />\n\n[disjoint-bones.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/27237341/disjoint-bones.zip)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4351266882/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]